      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded version of that section:\n\n\"Our notion of national security is no longer a zero-sum game; it's now inextricably linked to the global landscape. In an interconnected world, the notion of interior fences and overly restrictive borders isDubious at best. Rising external pressures can erode our domestic stability, lead to economic disruption, and test our social cohesion. The fact of the matter is, our security and prosperity are inextricably tied to the stability and prosperity of countries different from our own. Foreign aid is not just about altruism or taxes abroad; it's about safeguarding the expansible piece of global real estate in which we live, communicate, and operate. As fragile states falter, displaced populations threaten our borders, and festering conflicts push instability into our hard-earned backyard, international cooperation - including prudent and rational use of foreign aid - is the very lifeline that will ultimately keep us safe and prosperous in the century to come.",
